# Local path overrides. Every machine-specific path lives here, never in
# tracked code; config.local.example.R shows what goes in it.
config.local.R

# R session cruft
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
Rplots.pdf

# Generated grids. The driver writes them to output/<res>min/ (dir.basemaps in
# make_WFS_basemaps.R). The small Ecospace deliverables -- the depth grid and
# every habitat layer, as .asc/.prj/.csv plus a CHECKSUMS.md5 per resolution --
# are TRACKED so a regeneration shows in git diff and a downstream repo (GFISHER)
# can verify its copies. Figures, PDFs, GDAL sidecars and sections 3-5
# (management areas, ports, regions) stay ignored.
# git cannot re-include a file under an excluded directory, so the directories
# are opened one level at a time and only the wanted extensions negated.
output/*
!output/*min/
output/*min/*
!output/*min/CHECKSUMS.md5
!output/*min/depth/
!output/*min/habitat/
output/*min/habitat/*
!output/*min/habitat/sum1/
!output/*min/habitat/seagrass/
!output/*min/habitat/dbseabed/
!output/*min/habitat/gfisher/
!output/*min/habitat/artificial_reefs/
*.asc
*.prj
*.aux.xml
*.log
*.png
*.pdf
!output/*min/depth/*.asc
!output/*min/depth/*.prj
!output/*min/habitat/*/*.asc
!output/*min/habitat/*/*.prj
!output/*min/habitat/*/*.csv

# ...except the README figures, which are checked in deliberately.
!docs/img/*.png

# Source data. The whole tree is excluded, then three small folders are added
# back because they are either irreplaceable or awkward to re-source:
#   regions/          age0_survey_regions_5min_mod.asc is HAND-EDITED and exists
#                     nowhere else; the age-0 shapefile came from a Python
#                     digitizing step that is not reproducible in R
#   management_areas/ 8 small zips that are the definition of the areas
#   ports/            a specific FWC ReportCreator query (1985-2025, all
#                     species) that would have to be reconstructed exactly
#
# Still excluded, deliberately:
#   seagrass/         Seagrass_Statewide.shp alone is 230 MB, over GitHub's
#                     100 MB per-file hard limit
#   *.gdb/            275 MB, and FWRI-supplied - check redistribution terms
#   dbseabed/         downloads itself via fn.pull_dbseabed()
#   artificial_reefs/ source is marked REDACTED; check terms before publishing
data/*
!data/management_areas/
!data/ports/
!data/regions/

# The extension rules above still apply inside those folders, so undo them
# where the region inputs need to survive.
!data/regions/*.asc
!data/regions/*.prj
